# product.env -- the single source of product identity for THIS repo.
#
# scripts/init.sh writes the real product.env from your --product / --product-org
# / --domain / --engine-ref / --registry flags and PRUNES this .example. Every
# operational file (the root + per-surface Makefiles, scripts/*, CI) reads it
# and stays byte-identical to the template, so a later `git merge template/main`
# never conflicts on them. Values that a tool genuinely cannot read at runtime
# (a concept namespace in .memql, an ingress hostname, an image name) are the
# only things init.sh stamps into file contents.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, shell-sourceable (no spaces around =).

# Product name -- lowercase slug, ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$. Names the DSL namespace and
# prefixes every product image: <product>-dsl-bundle and one <product>-<surface>
# per client surface under clients/ (see clients/README.md).
PRODUCT=__PRODUCT__

# GitHub org/user that owns this product repo (and, if you publish one, the SDK
# package scope). Not the engine org -- znasllc-io stays literal everywhere.
PRODUCT_ORG=__PRODUCT_ORG__

# The domain this cluster is served at (mkcert wildcard locally). The stack
# serves https://identity.$DOMAIN, https://bff.$DOMAIN, https://app.$DOMAIN.
# It must MATCH the domain the sibling engine cluster was brought up with
# (`make up DOMAIN=...` over there): the engine Application owns identity, and
# every node derives its issuer / CORS origins / OAuth redirect URIs from the
# one MEMQL_DOMAIN the cluster was seeded with. The default on both sides is
# memql.localhost, an RFC 6761 loopback name. This is also the cloud
# public-entry placeholder you set on the cloud overlay at activation time.
DOMAIN=__DOMAIN__

# Engine ref this product ships against: a git tag/branch of znasllc-io/memql.
# The local stack runs `make -C ../memql up` at this ref; the overlays pin the
# engine node images to it. init.sh DEFAULTS this to the latest engine RELEASE
# tag, resolved over the network at stamp time (falls back to "main" with a loud
# warning when offline). Pass --engine-ref=<tag> to pin a specific ref instead.
# To bump an already-stamped product: edit ENGINE_REF here AND the engine image
# pins under deploy/k8s/overlays/*, then re-run CI. A flagless init.sh re-run
# PRESERVES this pin -- it never re-resolves over the network.
ENGINE_REF=__ENGINE_REF__

# Container registry that hosts the product's bundle + client-surface images
# (e.g. ghcr.io/acme-io or acme.azurecr.io). EMPTY = local-only: images build
# and import into k3d by bare name, the cloud overlay stays unshipped. The local
# overlay works with no registry at all.
REGISTRY=
